{"subtask_id":4,"findings":"Activity frequency profiles differ substantially between Application and Offer objects. Applications have 239595 total object-related events distributed over 10 activities, with the highest share at A_Validating (38816, 16.2%) and repeated lifecycle milestones A_Create Application, A_Concept, and A_Accepted each occurring 31509 times (13.15%). Offers have 193849 total object-related events over 8 activities, dominated by early offer creation/sending: O_Create Offer and O_Created each occur 42995 times (22.18%), and O_Sent (mail and online) occurs 39707 times (20.48%). This indicates the offer perspective is more concentrated in offer creation and dispatch activities, whereas the application perspective includes more validation and state-change repetitions such as A_Validating, A_Incomplete, A_Submitted, and A_Pending.

Interaction pattern analysis shows no direct Application-Offer co-occurrence at the event level for the inspected activities. All Application activities analyzed co-occurred exclusively with Case_R, with exactly 1 Application and 1 Case_R per event. All Offer activities analyzed co-occurred exclusively with Case_R and Offer, with exactly 1 Offer and 1 Case_R per event. Thus, Application-Offer interaction appears to be mediated structurally through object-to-object relationships and/or the shared Case_R object, rather than direct multi-object events containing both Application and Offer.

